<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
        The dark counterparts of the wait screen's three values (FR-031, research R7).

        **Not optional.** Without this file the wait screen is a full-brightness field at night -
        on the one screen in the app designed not to be noticed, and the one screen a user is most
        likely to meet in a dark room. It is also the difference between a matched starting window
        and a white flash in dark mode (manual case M5.2).

        This is the ONLY surface in the app that follows the device's light/dark setting in
        Phase 1. The four in-app screens are pinned to light until Phase 3 builds a reviewed dark
        palette (FR-008). That asymmetry is deliberate: a bright app in dark mode is a nuisance,
        a white flash at 2am is a defect.

        #14120E is the warm near-black the light ground implies, not a neutral grey, so the two
        modes read as the same product. Measured contrast: message on background 5.09:1, rule on
        background 5.96:1 - both clear of the 4.5:1 floor. The accent is unchanged in both modes;
        it reads on either ground.
    -->
    <color name="wait_background">#FF14120E</color>
    <color name="wait_text">#FF8A857A</color>
    <color name="wait_rule">#FFC9821F</color>
</resources>
